{"name":"Symbolic","hex":"#b29ead","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"symbolic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to a symbol.","Implicitly representing or referring to another thing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbolic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Symbol","blocks":[{"text":"A symbol is a mark, sign, or word that indicates, signifies, or is understood as representing an idea, object, relationship, or mathematical formula. Symbols allow people to go beyond what is known or seen by creating linkages between otherwise different concepts and experiences. All communication is achieved through the use of symbols: for example, a red octagon is a common symbol for \"STOP\"; on maps, blue lines often represent rivers; and a red rose often symbolizes love and compassion. Numerals are symbols for numbers; letters of an alphabet may be symbols for certain phonemes; and personal names are symbols representing individuals. The academic study of symbols is called semiotics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Blank_stop_sign_octagon.svg/330px-Blank_stop_sign_octagon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbol","wikidata":"Q80071"},{"title":"Symbolic (Death album)","blocks":[{"text":"Symbolic is the sixth studio album by American death metal band Death, released on March 21, 1995, by Roadrunner Records. The album marked a shift towards melodic death metal, while still retaining elements of technical death metal. It is the only album to feature Bobby Koelble and Kelly Conlon on guitar and bass, respectively, and the second and last album to feature drummer Gene Hoglan."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Symbolic_Album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_(Death_album)","wikidata":"Q919092"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png/500px-Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png/1280px-Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png/500px-Terminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The string \"the dog ate the bone\" was created using production rules that replaced nonterminal with terminal symbols.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerminal_and_non-terminal_symbols_example.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e3/Symbolic_Album.jpg/250px-Symbolic_Album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Symbolic_Album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e3/Symbolic_Album.jpg/250px-Symbolic_Album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASymbolic_Album.jpg"}],"sounds":{"symbolic":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/En-us-symbolic.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e1/En-us-symbolic.ogg/En-us-symbolic.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-symbolic.wav?utm_source=en.wiktion